hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15466","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Saib ibn Umar, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Saib narrated to me that Abd Allah ibn al-Saib used to lead Abd Allah ibn Abbas and station him at the third crevice toward the door toward the stone. So I said, meaning the speaker is Ibn Abbas, to Abd Allah ibn al-Saib: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand here, or pray here? So he said: Yes. So Ibn Abbas stood and prayed."
"15467","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of the conquest and placed his sandals to his left. Abd Allah said: I heard this hadith from my father three times."
"15468","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makhzumi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began prayer on the day of the conquest at Fajr, and recited Surat al-Muminin. So when he reached the mention of Musa and Harun, a cough seized him, so he bowed."
"15469","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan and Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and Abd Allah ibn al-Musayyab al-Abidi informed me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Subh in Makkah. He said: So he began a surah, and when he reached the mention of Musa and Harun, or the mention of Isa, Muhammad ibn Abbad doubts, and they differed against him, a cough seized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he bowed. He said: And Ibn al-Saib was present at that."
"15470","Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh narrated to us, both said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan and Abd Allah ibn Amr, Rawh said: Ibn al-As, and Abd Allah ibn al-Musayyab al-Abidi informed me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Subh in Makkah, and began Surat al-Muminin, until when the mention of Musa and Harun came, or the mention of Isa, Rawh said: Muhammad ibn Abbad doubts, and they differed against him, a cough seized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he omitted and bowed. He said: And Abd Allah ibn al-Saib was present at that."
"15471","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray before Zuhr, after the decline, four, and he said: The gates of heaven are opened, so I like to send forth in them a righteous deed."
"15472","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to me a hadith he raised to Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan and Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, he said: I attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest, and he prayed facing the Kabah. So he removed his sandals and placed them to his left. Then he began Surat al-Muminin. So when the mention of Isa or Musa came, a cough seized him, so he bowed."
"15473","Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh narrated to us, both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Yahya ibn Ubayd, the freedman of al-Saib, narrated to me that his father informed him that Abd Allah ibn al-Saib informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying between the corner of Banu Jumah and the Black Corner: Our Lord, give us in this world good, and in the Hereafter good, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"15474","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Ubayd informed me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting between the Yemeni Corner and the Stone: Our Lord, give us in this world good, and in the Hereafter good, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr and Rawh said in this hadith: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying between the corner of Banu Jumah and the Black Corner: Our Lord, give us."
"15475","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan and Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and Abd Allah ibn al-Musayyab al-Abidi informed me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Subh, and began Surat al-Muminin, until when the mention of Musa and Harun came, or the mention of Isa, Muhammad ibn Abbad doubted, they differed against him, a cough seized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he omitted and bowed. He said: And Ibn al-Saib was present at that."
